# Unreal assets (*.uasset, *.umap) are committed through Git LFS (.gitattributes): the generated
# materials, imported props, cards and maps travel with the repo so the project opens ready to play
# (unreal/Content/Python/shortstack_setup.py still regenerates them when their sources change).
# The Back Room's MetaHumans (~5.4 GB of Epic MetaHuman source assets) stay local: the repo is public
# and Epic's license doesn't allow redistributing them. Rebuild them with
# unreal/Content/Python/backroom_cast.py (needs an Epic account sign-in for the MetaHuman cloud).
unreal/Content/ShortStack/Cast/
__pycache__/
# Intermediate textures and review renders from art/blender/build.py
art/build/
